// Title: UAC Secure Desktop Prompt Disabled
// Sigma ID: 0d7ceeef-3539-4392-8953-3dc664912714
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2024-05-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects when an attacker tries to change User Account Control (UAC) elevation request
//   destination via the "PromptOnSecureDesktop" value. The "PromptOnSecureDesktop" setting
//   specifically determines whether UAC prompts are displayed on the secure desktop. The secure
//   desktop is a separate desktop environment that's isolated from other processes running on the
//   system. It's designed to prevent malicious software from intercepting or tampering with UAC
//   prompts. When "PromptOnSecureDesktop" is set to 0, UAC prompts are displayed on the user's
//   current desktop instead of the secure desktop. This reduces the level of security because it
//   potentially exposes the prompts to manipulation by malicious software.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/7e11e9b79583545f208a6dc3fa062f2ed443d999/atomics/T1548.002/T1548.002.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_uac_disable_secure_desktop_prompt.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\PromptOnSecureDesktop" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"
